@page "/"
<PageTitle>GeoShift — Convert, Merge &amp; Clean Data</PageTitle>

<section class="gs-hero">
    <div class="gs-hero-glow"></div>
    <div class="gs-container gs-hero-inner">
        <div class="gs-eyebrow"><span class="gs-eyebrow-dot"></span> DATA MIGRATION, MADE SIMPLE</div>
        <h1>Messy data in.<br /><span>Useful data out.</span></h1>
        <p class="gs-hero-lead">Convert geographic files, combine spreadsheets, recover missing information, and resolve duplicates—with a clear review process and downloadable audit trail.</p>
        <div class="gs-hero-actions">
            <a class="gs-btn gs-btn-primary" href="/migrate">Clean &amp; merge data <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="gs-btn gs-btn-ghost" href="/analyze">Convert KML / KMZ <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="gs-hero-tags"><span>✓ CSV &amp; Excel</span><span>✓ KML &amp; KMZ</span><span>✓ Review before combining</span><span>✓ Export with an audit trail</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="gs-orbit gs-orbit-one"></div><div class="gs-orbit gs-orbit-two"></div>
</section>

<section class="gs-container gs-features" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="gs-section-heading">
        <div class="gs-eyebrow">CHOOSE YOUR WORKSPACE</div>
        <h2>Two tools. One straightforward workflow.</h2>
        <p>Start with the job you need done. Your original files remain unchanged.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="gs-feature-grid gs-workspace-grid">
        <article class="gs-feature">
            <span class="gs-feature-icon">01</span>
            <h3>Clean &amp; merge data</h3>
            <p>Bring CSV and Excel files together, match columns, review duplicate records, recover missing values, and export the results.</p>
            <a class="gs-feature-link" href="/migrate">Open migration workspace ↗</a>
        </article>
        <article class="gs-feature">
            <span class="gs-feature-icon">02</span>
            <h3>Convert geographic files</h3>
            <p>Analyze Google Earth KML and KMZ files, inspect placemarks and attributes, then convert supported point data to CSV.</p>
            <a class="gs-feature-link" href="/analyze">Open converter ↗</a>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>